    {'colophon': "atha dvādaśo'dhyāyaḥ", 'gloss': 'Here begins the twelfth adhyāya.'},
    {'heading': '12.1 · The deities of the sky; the Aśvins'},
    {'padas': ['athāto dyusthānā devatāḥ | tāsāmaśvinau prathamāgāminau bhavataḥ | aśvinau yadvyaśnuvāte sarvam | rasenānyaḥ | jyotiṣānyaḥ | aśvairaśvināvityaurṇavābhaḥ |', 'tatkāvaśvinau | dyāvāpṛthivyāvityeke | ahorātrāvityeke | sūryācandramasāvityeke | rājānau puṇyakṛtāvityaitihāsikāḥ | tayoḥ kāla ūrdhvamardharātrātprakāśībhāvasyānuviṣṭambham | anutamobhāgo hi madhyamo jyotirbhāga ādityaḥ |', 'tayoreṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'Now the deities of the sky, first the Aśvins, "who pervade all", one with juice, one with light, or (Aurṇavābha) "having horses". Who are they? Heaven and earth, day and night, sun and moon, or two holy kings (the story-tellers). Their time is after midnight, as light begins to break.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.2 · The two of one time'},
    {'padas': ["vasātiṣu sma caratho'sitau petvāviva |", 'kadedamaśvinā yuvamabhi devāṁ agacchatam ||', 'iti sā nigadavyākhyātā |', "tayoḥ samānakālayoḥ samānakarmaṇoḥ saṃstutaprāyayorasaṃstavenaiṣo'rdharco bhavati | vāsātyo anya ucyate | uṣaḥ putrastvanya iti |", 'tayoreṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.73.2 (or a like verse): you two wander among the dwellings like the black pair; when did you come to the gods? Half a verse treats them apart: one is called Vāsatya, the other son of Dawn.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.3 · Born here and there'},
    {'padas': ['iheha jātā samavāvaśītāmarepasā tanvā nāmabhiḥ svaiḥ |', 'jiṣṇurvāmanyaḥ sumakhasya sūrirdivo anyaḥ subhagaḥ putra ūhe ||', "iha ceha ca jātau saṃstūyete pāpenālipyamānayā tanvā nāmabhiśca svaiḥ | jiṣṇurvāmanyaḥ sumahato balasyerayitā madhyamaḥ | divo'nyaḥ subhagaḥ putra ūhyata ādityaḥ |", 'tayoreṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.181.4: born here and there, they are praised with spotless bodies and names; the victorious one is the middle god, the other the fortunate son of the sky, the sun.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.4 · The early-yoked'},
    {'padas': ['prātaryujā vi bodhayāśvināveha gacchatām |', 'asya somasya pītaye ||', 'prātaryoginau vibodhayāśvināvihāgacchatāmasya somasya pānāya |', 'tayoreṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.22.1: wake the two early-yoked Aśvins; let them come to drink this soma.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.5 · Worship them at dawn; Uṣas'},
    {'padas': ['prātaryajadhvamaśvinā hinota na sāyamasti devayā ajuṣṭam |', 'utānyo asmadyajate vi cāvaḥ pūrvaḥpūrvo yajamāno vanīyān ||', "prātaryajadhvamaśvinau prahiṇuta na sāyamasti devejyā ajuṣṭametat | apyanyo'smadyajate vi cāvaḥ | pūrvaḥpūrvo yajamāno vanīyānvanayitṛtamaḥ |", 'tayoḥ kālaḥ sūryodayaparyantaḥ | tasminnanyā devatā opyante |', 'uṣā vaṣṭeḥ kāntikarmaṇaḥ | ucchateritarā mādhyamikā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.77.2: worship the Aśvins at dawn; the evening is not for the gods. Their time lasts till sunrise. Uṣas, dawn, "the longing one"; the other dawn, of the mid-air, from "to shine".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.6 · Dawn'},
    {'padas': ['uṣastaccitramā bharāsmabhyaṃ vājinīvati |', 'yena tokaṃ ca tanayaṃ ca dhāmahe ||', 'uṣastat [ citraṃ ] cāyanīyaṃ [ maṃhanīyaṃ ] dhanamāhara | asmabhyamannavati | yena putrāṃśca pautrāṃśca dadhīmahi |', 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 6 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.92.13: bring us that bright wealth, dawn, by which we may nourish sons and grandsons.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.7 · The dawns; Sūryā'},
    {'padas': ['etā u tyā uṣasaḥ ketumakrata pūrve ardhe rajaso bhānumañjate |', "niṣkṛṇvānā āyudhānīva dhṛṣṇavaḥ prati gāvo'ruṣīryanti mātaraḥ ||", "etāstā uṣasaḥ ketumakṛṣata prajñānam | ekasyā eva pūjanārthe bahuvacanaṃ syāt | pūrve'rdhe'ntarikṣalokasya samañjate bhānunā | niṣkṛṇvānā āyudhānīva dhṛṣṇavaḥ | nirityeṣa samityetasya sthāne |", 'emīdeṣāṃ niṣkṛtaṃ jāriṇīva |', 'ityapi nigamo bhavati |', 'prati yanti | gāvo gamanāt | aruṣīrārocanāt | mātaro bhāso nirmātryaḥ |', 'sūryā sūryasya patnī | eṣaivābhisṛṣṭakālatamā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 7 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 1.92.1: these dawns have raised their banner in the eastern half of the sky. The plural honours one. Sūryā, the sun's wife.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.8 · Sūryā's bridal car; Vṛṣākapāyī"},
    {'padas': ['sukiṃśukaṃ śalmaliṃ viśvarūpaṃ hiraṇyavarṇaṃ suvṛtaṃ sucakram |', 'ā roha sūrye amṛtasya lokaṃ syonaṃ patye vahatuṃ kṛṇuṣva ||', 'sukāśanaṃ śannamalaṃ sarvarūpam | api vopamārthe syāt | sukiṃśukamiva śalmalimiti | kiṃśukaṃ kraṃśateḥ prakāśayatikarmaṇaḥ | śalmaliḥ suśaro bhavati | śaravānvā | āroha sūrye amṛtasya lokamudakasya | sukhaṃ patye vahatuṃ kuruṣva |', 'savitā sūryāṃ prāyacchatsomāya rājñe prajāpataye vā |', 'iti ca brāhmaṇam |', 'vṛṣākapāyī vṛṣākapeḥ patnī | eṣaivābhisṛṣṭakālatamā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 8 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.85.20: mount, Sūryā, the fair car of śalmali wood, golden, many-formed; make your husband a happy bridal. "Savitṛ gave Sūryā to King Soma or to Prajāpati". Vṛṣākapāyī, Vṛṣākapi\'s wife.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.9 · Vṛṣākapāyī; Saraṇyū'},
    {'padas': ['vṛṣākapāyi revati suputra ādu susnuṣe |', 'ghasatta indra ukṣaṇaḥ priyaṃ kācitkaraṃ havirviśvasmādindra uttaraḥ ||', 'vṛṣākapāyi revati suputre madhyamena susnuṣe mādhyamikayā vācā | snuṣā sādhusādinīti vā | sādhusāninīti vā | svapatyaṃ tatsanotīti vā |', 'prāśnātu ta indra ukṣaṇa etānmādhyamikāntsaṃstyāyān | ukṣaṇa ukṣatervṛddhikarmaṇaḥ | ukṣantyudakeneti vā | priyaṃ kuruṣva sukhācayakaraṃ haviḥ [ sukhakaraṃ haviḥ ] | sarvasmād ya indra uttarastametadbrūma ādityam |', 'saraṇyūḥ saraṇāt | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 9 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.86.13: rich Vṛṣākapāyī with good sons and daughters-in-law; let Indra eat your bulls. Snuṣā, ukṣan. Saraṇyū.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.10 · Saraṇyū and the story of her twins'},
    {'padas': ['apāgūhannamṛtāṃ martyebhyaḥ kṛtvī savarṇāmadadurvivasvate |', 'utāśvināvabharadyattadāsīdajahādu dvā mithunā saraṇyūḥ ||', 'apāgūhannamṛtāṃ martyebhyaḥ kṛtvī savarṇāmadadurvivasvate | apyaśvinābharat yattadāsīt | ajahād dvau mithunau saraṇyūḥ |', 'madhyamaṃ ca mādhyamikāṃ ca vācamiti nairuktāḥ | yamaṃ ca yamīṃ cetyaitihāsikāḥ |', "tatretihāsamācakṣate | tvāṣṭrī saraṇyūrvivasvata ādityādyamau mithunau janayāñcakāra | sa savarṇāmanyāṃ pratinidhāyāśvaṃ rūpaṃ kṛtvā pradudrāva | sa vivasvānāditya āśvameva rūpaṃ kṛtvā tāmanusṛtya saṃbabhūva | tato'śvinau jajñāte | savarṇāyāṃ manuḥ | tadabhivādinyeṣargbhavati"], 'num': '|| 10 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 10.17.2: they hid the immortal from mortals and gave her likeness to Vivasvat; she bore the Aśvins and left both pairs. The story: Saraṇyū, Tvaṣṭṛ's daughter, bore twins to Vivasvat, left a likeness in her place and fled as a mare; Vivasvat followed as a horse; the Aśvins were born, and Manu of the likeness.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.11 · Tvaṣṭṛ's daughter's wedding"},
    {'padas': ['tvaṣṭā duhitre vahatuṃ kṛṇotītīdaṃ viśvaṃ bhuvanaṃ sameti |', 'yamasya mātā paryuhyamānā maho jāyā vivasvato nanāśa ||', "tvaṣṭā duhiturvahanaṃ karotīti [ idaṃ viśvaṃ bhuvanaṃ sameti ] | imāni ca sarvāṇi bhūtānyabhisamāgacchanti | yamasya mātā paryuhyamānā mahato jāyā vivasvato nanāśa | rātrirādityasya | ādityodaye'ntardhīyate"], 'num': '|| 11 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 10.17.1: Tvaṣṭṛ makes a wedding for his daughter, and all the world comes; Yama's mother, being wed, vanished: night, which vanishes at sunrise.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.12 · Savitṛ'},
    {'padas': ['savitā vyākhyātaḥ | tasya kālo yadā dyaurapahatatamaskākīrṇaraśmirbhavati |', 'tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 12 ||', 'gloss': "Savitṛ's time is when the sky is cleared of darkness and filled with rays.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.13 · Savitṛ who puts on all forms; Bhaga'},
    {'padas': ['viśvā rūpāṇi prati muñcate kaviḥ prāsāvīdbhadraṃ dvipade catuṣpade |', "vi nākamakhyatsavitā vareṇyo'nu prayāṇamuṣaso vi rājati ||", 'sarvāṇi prajñānāni pratimuñcate medhāvī | kaviḥ krāntadarśano bhavati | kavatervā | prasuvati bhadraṃ dvipādbhyaśca catuṣpādbhyaśca | vyacikhyapannākaṃ savitā varaṇīyaḥ | prayāṇamanūṣaso virājati |', 'adhorāmaḥ sāvitraḥ |', 'iti paśusamāmnāye vijñāyate |', "kasmātsāmānyāditi | adhastāttadvelāyāṃ tamo bhavatyetasmātsāmānyāt | adhastādrāmo'dhastātkṛṣṇaḥ | kasmātsāmānyāditi | agniṃ citvā na rāmāmupeyāt | rāmā ramaṇāyopeyate na dharmāya | kṛṣṇajātīyaitasmātsāmānyāt |", 'kṛkavākuḥ sāvitraḥ |', 'iti paśusamāmnāye vijñāyate |', 'kasmātsāmānyāditi | kālānuvādaṃ parītya | kṛkavākoḥ pūrvaṃ śabdānukaraṇaṃ vaceruttaram |', 'bhago vyākhyātaḥ | tasya kālaḥ prāgutsarpaṇāt | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 13 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.81.2: the poet puts on all forms, brings good to two-footed and four-footed; Savitṛ lit the vault. The animal lists: the black-bellied ram and the cock belong to Savitṛ, and why. Bhaga, whose time is before sunrise.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.14 · Bhaga; Sūrya'},
    {'padas': ['prātarjitaṃ bhagamugraṃ huvema vayaṃ putramaditeryo vidhartā |', 'ādhraścidyaṃ manyamānasturaścidrājā cidyaṃ bhagaṃ bhakṣītyāha ||', 'prātarjitaṃ bhagamugraṃ hvayema vayaṃ putramaditeryo vidhārayitā sarvasya | ādhraścidyaṃ manyamāna āḍhyālurdaridraḥ | turaścit | tura iti yamanāma | taratervā | tvaratervā | tvarayā tūrṇagatiryamaḥ | rājā cidyaṃ bhagaṃ bhakṣītyāha |', 'andho bhaga ityāhuranutsṛpto na dṛśyate | prāśitramasyākṣiṇī nirjaghāna |', 'iti ca brāhmaṇam |', 'janaṃ bhago gacchati |', 'iti [ vā ] vijñāyate |', 'janaṃ gacchatyāditya udayena |', 'sūryaḥ sartervā | suvatervā | svīryatervā | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 14 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 7.41.2: let us call Bhaga the early winner, son of Aditi, whom poor and king alike pray to for a share. Tura, Yama. "Bhaga is blind"; "Bhaga goes to the people". Sūrya, the sun.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.15 · The sun's banners"},
    {'padas': ['udu tyaṃ jātavedasaṃ devaṃ vahanti ketavaḥ |', 'dṛśe viśvāya sūryam ||', 'udvahanti taṃ jātavedasaṃ raśmayaḥ ketavaḥ | sarveṣāṃ bhūtānāṃ darśanāya sūryamiti | [ kamanyamādityādevamavakṣyat | ]', 'tasyaiṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 15 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.50.1: his rays carry up the god Jātavedas, the sun, for all to see.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.16 · The bright face of the gods; Pūṣan'},
    {'padas': ['citraṃ devānāmudagādanīkaṃ cakṣurmitrasya varuṇasyāgneḥ |', 'āprā dyāvāpṛthivī antarikṣaṃ sūrya ātmā jagatastasthuṣaśca ||', 'cāyanīyaṃ devānāmudagamadanīkam | khyānaṃ mitrasya varuṇasyāgneśca | āpūpurad dyāvāpṛthivyau cāntarikṣaṃ ca mahattvena [ tena ] | sūrya ātmā jaṅgamasya ca sthāvarasya ca |', 'atha yadraśmipoṣaṃ puṣyati tatpūṣā bhavati |', 'tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 16 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.115.1: the bright face of the gods has risen, the eye of Mitra, Varuṇa, Agni; the sun is the self of all that moves and stands. When he nourishes the rays, he is Pūṣan.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.17 · Pūṣan's two forms"},
    {'padas': ['śukraṃ te anyadyajataṃ te anyadviṣurūpe ahanī dyaurivāsi |', 'viśvā hi māyā avasi svadhāvo bhadrā te pūṣanniha rātirastu ||', 'śukraṃ te anyat | lohitaṃ te anyat | yajataṃ te anyat | yajñiyaṃ te anyat | viṣamarūpe te ahanī karma dyauriva cāsi | sarvāṇi prajñānānyavasi | annavan | bhājanavatī te pūṣanniha dattirastu |', 'tasyaiṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 17 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 6.58.1: one form of yours is bright, one worshipful; you are like the sky in day and night; may your gift be favourable here, Pūṣan.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.18 · Pūṣan, lord of the paths; Viṣṇu'},
    {'padas': ['pathaspathaḥ paripatiṃ vacasyā kāmena kṛto abhyānaḷarkam |', 'sa no rāsacchurudhaścandrāgrā dhiyaṃdhiyaṃ sīṣadhāti pra pūṣā ||', "pathaspathaḥ | adhipatim | vacanena | kāmena kṛtaḥ | abhyānaḷarkam | abhyāpanno'rkamiti vā | sa no dadātu cāyanīyāgrāṇi dhanāni | karmakarma ca naḥ prasādhayatu pūṣeti |", 'atha yadviṣito bhavati tadviṣṇurbhavati | viṣṇurviśatervā | vyaśnotervā |', 'tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 18 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 6.49.8: Pūṣan, lord of every path; may he give bright riches and further every thought. When he pervades, he is Viṣṇu.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.19 · Viṣṇu's three steps"},
    {'padas': ['idaṃ viṣṇurvi cakrame tredhā ni dadhe padam |', 'samūḷhamasya pāṃsure ||', "yadidaṃ kiṃ ca tadvikramate viṣṇuḥ | tridhā nidhatte padam | [ tredhābhāvāya | ] pṛthivyāmantarikṣe divīti śākapūṇiḥ | samārohaṇe viṣṇupade gayaśirasītyaurṇavābhaḥ | samūḷhamasya [ pāṃsure ] pyāyane'ntarikṣe padaṃ na dṛśyate | api vopamārthe syāt | samūḷhamasya pāṃsula iva padaṃ na dṛśyata iti | pāṃsavaḥ pādaiḥ sūyanta iti vā | pannāḥ śerata iti vā | paṃsanīyā bhavantīti vā"], 'num': '|| 19 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.22.17: Viṣṇu strode over this; three times he set his foot; it is hidden in his dust. On earth, mid-air and sky (Śākapūṇi), or at the rising, the zenith and Gayaśiras (Aurṇavābha); pāṃsu.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.20 · Viśvānara'},
    {'padas': ['viśvānaro vyākhyātaḥ | tasyaiṣa nipāto bhavatyaindryāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 20 ||', 'gloss': 'Viśvānara appears in passing in a verse to Indra (Ṛgveda 8.68.4).', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.21 · Viśvānara's lord; Varuṇa"},
    {'padas': ['viśvānarasya vaspatimanānatasya śavasaḥ |', 'evaiśca carṣaṇīnāmūtī huve rathānām ||', 'viśvānarasyādityasya | anānatasya | śavaso mahato balasya | evaiśca kāmairayanairavanairvā | carṣaṇīnāṃ manuṣyāṇām | ūtyā ca pathā rathānām | indramasminyajñe hvayāmi |', 'varuṇo vyākhyātaḥ | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 21 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 8.68.4: I call the lord of Viśvānara's unbending might for help. Varuṇa.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.22 · The eye with which you see'},
    {'padas': ['yenā pāvaka cakṣasā bhuraṇyantaṃ janāṁ anu |', 'tvaṃ varuṇa paśyasi ||', 'bhuraṇyuriti kṣipranāma | bhuraṇyuḥ śakuniḥ | bhūrimadhvānaṃ nayati | svargasya lokasyāpi voḷhā | tatsaṃpātī bhuraṇyuḥ | anena pāvakakhyānena | bhuraṇyantaṃ janāṁ anu | tvaṃ varuṇa paśyasi | tatte vayaṃ stuma iti vākyaśeṣaḥ |', 'api vottarasyām'], 'num': '|| 22 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.50.6: with that eye, purifier, with which you look on the busy people, Varuṇa; the sentence is completed "we praise it". Bhuraṇyu. Or with the next verse.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.23 · With the next verse'},
    {'padas': ['yenā pāvaka cakṣasā bhuraṇyantaṃ janāṁ anu |', 'tvaṃ varuṇa paśyasi ||', 'vi dyāmeṣi rajaspṛthvahā mimāno aktubhiḥ |', 'paśyañjanmāni sūrya ||', "vyeṣi dyām | rajaśca | pṛthu mahāntaṃ lokam | ahāni ca mimāno'ktubhī rātribhiḥ saha | paśyañjanmāni jātāni sūrya |", 'api vā pūrvasyām'], 'num': '|| 23 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.50.7: you cross the sky and the wide region, measuring the days with the nights, watching the generations, sun.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.24 · With the previous verse'},
    {'padas': ['yenā pāvaka cakṣasā bhuraṇyantaṃ janāṁ anu |', 'tvaṃ varuṇa paśyasi ||', 'pratyaṅ devānāṃ viśaḥ pratyaṅṅudeṣi mānuṣān |', 'pratyaṅ viśvaṃ svardṛśe ||', 'pratyaṅṅidaṃ sarvam | [ udeṣi | pratyaṅṅidaṃ jyotirucyate | pratyaṅṅidaṃ sarvam ] ( idam ) abhivipaśyasīti |', 'api vaitasyāmeva'], 'num': '|| 24 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.50.5: you rise facing the clans of gods and men, facing all, that the sky be seen.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.25 · Or by itself; Keśin'},
    {'padas': ['yenā pāvaka cakṣasā bhuraṇyantaṃ janāṁ anu |', 'tvaṃ varuṇa paśyasi ||', 'tena no janānabhivipaśyasi |', 'keśī keśā raśmayaḥ | taistadvānbhavati | kāśanādvā | [ prakāśanādvā | ]', 'tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 25 ||', 'gloss': 'Or the verse stands alone: "with it you look on our people". Keśin, "the long-haired", the sun with his rays.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.26 · Keśin'},
    {'padas': ['keśyagniṃ keśī viṣaṃ keśī bibharti rodasī |', 'keśī viśvaṃ svardṛśe keśīdaṃ jyotirucyate ||', 'keśyagniṃ ca viṣaṃ ca | viṣamityudakanāma | viṣṇāteḥ | [ vipūrvasya snāteḥ śuddhyarthasya | ] vipūrvasya vā sacateḥ | dyāvāpṛthivyau ca dhārayati | keśīdaṃ sarvamidamabhivipaśyati | keśīdaṃ jyotirucyata ityādityamāha |', 'athāpyete itare jyotiṣī keśinī ucyete | dhūmenāgniḥ | rajasā ca madhyamaḥ |', 'tayoreṣā sādhāraṇā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 26 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.136.1: the long-haired holds fire, the long-haired holds water, the long-haired holds heaven and earth; he is called this light. The other two lights too are long-haired, Agni with smoke, the middle god with dust.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.27 · The three long-haired ones; Vṛṣākapi'},
    {'padas': ['trayaḥ keśina ṛtuthā vi cakṣate saṃvatsare vapata eka eṣām |', 'viśvameko abhi caṣṭe śacībhirdhrājirekasya dadṛśe na rūpam ||', "trayaḥ keśina ṛtuthā vicakṣate | kālekāle'bhivipaśyanti | saṃvatsare vapata eka eṣām | ityagniḥ pṛthivīṃ dahati | sarvameko'bhivipaśyati karmabhirādityaḥ | gatirekasya dṛśyate na rūpaṃ madhyamasya |", 'atha yad raśmibhirabhiprakampayanneti tad vṛṣākapirbhavati | vṛṣākampanaḥ |', 'tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 27 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.44: three long-haired ones appear in season: one shears the earth in the year (Agni), one looks on all with powers (the sun), the motion of one is seen, not his form (the middle god). Vṛṣākapi, the sun shaking with his rays.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.28 · Vṛṣākapi; Yama'},
    {'padas': ['punarehi vṛṣākape suvitā kalpayāvahai |', "ya eṣa svapnanaṃśano'stameṣi pathā punaḥ |", 'viśvasmādindra uttaraḥ ||', "punarehi vṛṣākape suprasūtāni vaḥ karmāṇi kalpayāvahai | ya eṣa svapnanaṃśanaḥ | svapnānnāśayati | āditya udayena | so'stameṣi pathā punaḥ | sarvasmād ya indra uttarastametad brūma ādityam |", 'yamo vyākhyātaḥ | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 28 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.86.21: come again, Vṛṣākapi; you who destroy sleep go home by the path again. Yama.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.29 · Yama under the leafy tree; Aja Ekapād'},
    {'padas': ['yasminvṛkṣe supalāśe devaiḥ saṃ pibate yamaḥ |', 'atrā no viśpatiḥ pitā purāṇāṁ anu venati ||', 'yasminvṛkṣe supalāśe sthāne vṛtakṣaye vā | api vopamārthe syāt | vṛkṣa iva supalāśa iti | vṛkṣo vraścanāt | palāśaṃ palāśanāt | devaiḥ saṃgacchate yamaḥ | raśmibhirādityaḥ | tatra naḥ sarvasya pātā vā pālayitā vā purāṇānanukāmayeta |', "aja ekapādajana ekaḥ pādaḥ | ekena pādena pātīti vā | ekena pādena pibatīti vā | eko'sya pāda iti vā |", 'ekaṃ pādaṃ notkhidati |', 'ityapi nigamo bhavati | tasyaiṣa nipāto bhavati vaiśvadevyāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 29 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.135.1: under the leafy tree where Yama drinks with the gods, our father, lord of the clans, longs for the ancients. Aja Ekapād, "the one-footed unborn".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.30 · Aja Ekapād; Pṛthivī'},
    {'padas': ['pāvīravī tanyaturekapādajo divo dhartā sindhurāpaḥ samudriyaḥ |', 'viśve devāsaḥ śṛṇavanvacāṃsi me sarasvatī saha dhībhiḥ purandhyā ||', 'paviḥ śalyo bhavati | yadvipunāti kāyam | tadvat | pavīramāyudham | tadvānindraḥ pavīravān |', 'atitasthau pavīravān |', "ityapi nigamo bhavati | tad devatā vākpāvīravī | pāvīravī ca divyā vāk | tanyatustanitrī vāco'nyasyāḥ | ajaścaikapād divo dhārayitā | sindhuśca | āpaśca samudriyāśca | sarve ca devāḥ | sarasvatī ca saha purandhyā stutyā | prayuktāni dhībhiḥ karmabhiryuktāni | śṛṇvantu vacanānīmānīti |", 'pṛthivī vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣa nipāto bhavatyaindrāgnyāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 30 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.65.13: Pāvīravī the thunderer, Aja Ekapād upholder of the sky, the river, the waters: let all the gods hear my words. Pavi, pavīravat. The earth, in an Indra-Agni verse.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.31 · The highest earth; Samudra'},
    {'padas': ['yadindrāgnī paramasyāṃ pṛthivyāṃ madhyamasyāmavamasyāmuta sthaḥ |', 'ataḥ pari vṛṣaṇāvā hi yātamathā somasya pibataṃ sutasya ||', 'iti sā nigadavyākhyātā |', 'samudro vyākhyātaḥ | tasyaiṣa nipāto bhavati pāvamānyāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 31 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.108.9: whether, Indra and Agni, you are on the highest, middle or lowest earth, come from there. Samudra, in a verse of the Pavamāna book.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.32 · The ocean'},
    {'padas': ['pavitravantaḥ pari vācamāsate pitaiṣāṃ pratno abhi rakṣati vratam |', 'mahaḥ samudraṃ varuṇastiro dadhe dhīrā icchekurdharuṇeṣvārabham ||', "pavitravanto raśmivanto mādhyamikā devagaṇāḥ paryāsate [ mādhyamikāṃ vācam ] | madhyamaḥ pitaiṣāṃ pratnaḥ purāṇo'bhirakṣati vrataṃ karma | mahaḥ samudraṃ varuṇastiro'ntardadhāti | atha dhīrāḥ śaknuvanti dharuṇeṣūdakeṣu karmaṇa ārabhamārabdhum |", 'aja ekapād vyākhyātaḥ | pṛthivī vyākhyātā | samudro vyākhyātaḥ | teṣāmeṣa nipāto bhavatyaparasyāṃ bahudevatāyāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 32 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 9.73.3: the bright ones sit round speech; their ancient father guards the law; Varuṇa hid the great ocean.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.33 · Ahi Budhnya, Aja Ekapād, earth, ocean together; Dadhyañc'},
    {'padas': ["uta no'hirbudhnyaḥ śṛṇotvaja ekapātpṛthivī samudraḥ |", 'viśve devā ṛtāvṛdho huvānāḥ stutā mantrāḥ kaviśastā avantu ||', "api ca no'hirbudhnyaḥ śṛṇotu | ajaścaikapātpṛthivī ca samudraśca sarve ca devāḥ | satyavṛdho vā | yajñavṛdho vā | hūyamānā mantraiḥ stutāḥ | mantrāḥ kaviśastāḥ | avantu | medhāviśastāḥ |", 'dadhyaṅ pratyakto dhyānamiti vā | pratyaktamasmindhyānamiti vā |', 'atharvā vyākhyātaḥ | manurmananāt | teṣāmeṣa nipāto bhavatyaindryāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 33 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.64.4 (or a like verse): may Ahi Budhnya hear us, Aja Ekapād, earth and ocean, all the gods. Dadhyañc, "toward whom meditation turns". Atharvan, Manu.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.34 · Atharvan, Manu and Dadhyañc'},
    {'padas': ['yāmatharvā manuṣpitā dadhyaṅ dhiyamatnata |', 'tasminbrahmāṇi pūrvathendra ukthā samagmatārcannanu svarājyam ||', "yāmatharvā ca | manuśca pitā mānavānām | dadhyaṅ ca | dhiyamataniṣata | tasminbrahmāṇi karmāṇi pūrvendra ukthāni ca saṃgacchantām | arcanyo'nūpāste svārājyam"], 'num': '|| 34 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.80.16: the thought that Atharvan, father Manu and Dadhyañc spread; in it the prayers and hymns met with Indra as of old.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.35 · The groups of the sky; the Ādityas'},
    {'padas': ['athāto dyusthānā devagaṇāḥ | teṣāmādityāḥ prathamāgāmino bhavanti | ādityā vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 35 ||', 'gloss': 'Now the groups of gods of the sky, first the Ādityas. Ṛgveda 2.27.1: I offer these songs dripping ghee to the Ādityas; let Mitra, Aryaman, Bhaga, Varuṇa, Dakṣa and Aṃśa hear.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.36 · The seven seers'},
    {'padas': ['imā gira ādityebhyo ghṛtasnūḥ sanādrājabhyo juhvā juhomi |', 'śṛṇotu mitro aryamā bhago nastuvijāto varuṇo dakṣo aṃśaḥ ||', "ghṛtasnūrghṛtaprasnāvinyaḥ | ghṛtaprasrāviṇyaḥ | [ ghṛtasāninyaḥ | ghṛtasāriṇyaḥ ] iti vā | āhutīrādityebhyaściraṃ juhvā juhomi | [ ciraṃ jīvanāya | ] ciraṃ rājabhya iti vā | śṛṇotu na imā giro mitraścāryamā ca bhagaśca bahujātaśca dhātā dakṣo varuṇo'ṃśaśca | aṃśo'ṃśunā vyākhyātaḥ |", 'sapta ṛṣayo vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 36 ||', 'gloss': 'The seven seers, already explained.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.37 · The seven seers in the body'},
    {'padas': ['sapta ṛṣayaḥ pratihitāḥ śarīre sapta rakṣanti sadamapramādam |', 'saptāpaḥ svapato lokamīyustatra jāgṛto asvapnajau satrasadau ca devau ||', "sapta ṛṣayaḥ pratihitāḥ śarīre | raśmaya āditye | sapta rakṣanti sadamapramādam | saṃvatsaramapramādyantaḥ | saptāpanāsta eva svapato lokamastamitamādityaṃ yanti | tatra jāgṛto'svapnajau satrasadau ca devau vāyvādityau | ityadhidaivatam |", "athādhyātmam | sapta ṛṣayaḥ pratihitāḥ śarīre | ṣaḍindriyāṇi vidyā saptamyātmani | sapta rakṣanti sadamapramādam | śarīramapramādyanti | saptāpanānīmānyeva svapato lokamastamitamātmānaṃ yanti | tatra jāgṛto'svapnajau satrasadau ca devau prājñaścātmā taijasaśca | ityātmagatimācaṣṭe |", 'teṣāmeṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 37 ||', 'gloss': 'Vājasaneyi 34.55: seven seers are set in the body and guard it unwearied: the rays in the sun, or the six senses and the mind in the self; two gods watch while it sleeps: wind and sun, or the knowing self and the radiant self.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.38 · The cup with its opening sideways'},
    {'padas': ['tiryagbilaścamasa ūrdhvabudhno yasminyaśo nihitaṃ viśvarūpam |', 'atrāsata ṛṣayaḥ sapta sākaṃ ye asya gopā mahato babhūvuḥ ||', 'tiryagbilaścamasa ūrdhvabandhana ūrdhvabodhano vā | yasminyaśo nihitaṃ viśvarūpam | atrāsata ṛṣayaḥ sapta sahādityaraśmayaḥ | ye asya gopā mahato babhūvuḥ | ityadhidaivatam |', 'athādhyātmam | tiryagbilaścamasa ūrdhvabandhana ūrdhvabodhano vā | yasminyaśo nihitaṃ viśvarūpam | atrāsata ṛṣayaḥ sapta sahendriyāṇi | yānyasya goptṝṇi mahato babhūvuḥ | ityātmagatimācaṣṭe |', 'devā vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 38 ||', 'gloss': 'Atharvaveda-like verse: a cup with its opening sideways and its base above, in which all glory is set; there sit the seven seers: the sun with its rays, or the head with the senses. The gods.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.39 · The gods' favour; the Viśvedevas"},
    {'padas': ['devānāṃ bhadrā sumatirṛjūyatāṃ devānāṃ rātirabhi no ni vartatām |', 'devānāṃ sakhyamupa sedimā vayaṃ devā na āyuḥ pra tirantu jīvase ||', 'devānāṃ vayaṃ [ sumatau ] kalyāṇyāṃ matau | ṛjugāminām | ṛtugāmināmiti vā | devānāṃ dānamabhi no nivartatām | devānāṃ sakhyamupasīdema vayam | devā na āyuḥ pravardhayantu ciraṃ jīvanāya |', 'viśvedevāḥ sarvedevāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 39 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.89.2: may the kind favour of the gods be with us; may the gods lengthen our life. The Viśvedevas, all the gods.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.40 · The All-gods; the Sādhyas'},
    {'padas': ['omāsaścarṣaṇīdhṛto viśve devāsa ā gata |', 'dāśvāṃso dāśuṣaḥ sutam ||', 'avitāro vā | avanīyā vā | manuṣyadhṛtaḥ sarve ca devā ihāgacchata | dattavantaḥ | dattavataḥ sutamiti |', 'tadetadekameva vaiśvadevaṃ gāyatraṃ tṛcaṃ daśatayīṣu vidyate | yattu kiṃcid bahudaivataṃ tad vaiśvadevānāṃ sthāne yujyate | yadeva viśvaliṅgamiti śākapūṇiḥ | anatyantagatastveṣa uddeśo bhavati |', 'babhrureko |', 'iti daśa dvipadā aliṅgāḥ | bhūtāṃśaḥ kāśyapa āśvinamekaliṅgam | abhitaṣṭīyaṃ sūktamekaliṅgam |', 'sādhyā devāḥ sādhanāt | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 40 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.3.7: come, All-gods, helpers, upholders of men. The one Vaiśvadeva triplet in the ten books; Śākapūṇi on what counts as Vaiśvadeva; the unlabelled two-pāda verses and others. The Sādhyas.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.41 · The Sādhyas; the Vasus'},
    {'padas': ['yajñena yajñamayajanta devāstāni dharmāṇi prathamānyāsan |', 'te ha nākaṃ mahimānaḥ sacanta yatra pūrve sādhyāḥ santi devāḥ ||', 'yajñena yajñamayajanta devāḥ | agnināgnimayajanta devāḥ |', 'agniḥ paśurāsīt | tamālabhanta | tenāyajanta |', 'iti ca brāhmaṇam |', 'tāni dharmāṇi prathamānyāsan | te ha nākaṃ mahimānaḥ saṃsevyanta | yatra pūrve sādhyāḥ santi devāḥ sādhanāḥ | dyusthāno devagaṇa iti nairuktāḥ | pūrvaṃ devayugamityākhyānam |', 'vasavo yad vivasate sarvam | agnirvasubhirvāsava iti samākhyā | tasmātpṛthivīsthānāḥ | indro vasubhirvāsava iti samākhyā | tasmānmadhyasthānāḥ | vasava ādityaraśmayo vivāsanāt | tasmād dyusthānāḥ |', 'teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 41 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.90.16: with sacrifice the gods sacrificed to sacrifice; those were the first laws; the great ones reached the vault where the former Sādhyas are. A group of the sky, say the etymologists; the former age of gods, say the story-tellers. The Vasus of earth, mid-air and sky.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.42 · The Vasus'},
    {'padas': ['sugā vo devāḥ sadanamakarma ya ājagmuḥ savanamidaṃ juṣāṇāḥ |', "jakṣivāṃsaḥ papivāṃsaśca viśve'sme dhatta vasavo vasūni ||", "svāgamanāni vo devāḥ supathānyakarma ya āgacchata savanānīmāni | juṣāṇāḥ khāditavantaḥ | pītavantaśca | sarve'smāsu dhatta vasavo vasūni |", 'teṣāmeṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 42 ||', 'gloss': 'Vājasaneyi verse: we have made easy paths for you, gods; eat and drink and give us wealth, Vasus.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.43 · The Vasus at play; the Vājins'},
    {'padas': ['jmayā atra vasavo ranta devā urāvantarikṣe marjayanta śubhrāḥ |', 'arvākpatha urujrayaḥ kṛṇudhvaṃ śrotā dūtasya jagmuṣo no asya ||', "jmayā atra vasavo'ramanta devāḥ | jmā pṛthivī | tasyāṃ bhavā urau cāntarikṣe marjayanta gamayanta ramayanta | śubhrāḥ śobhamānāḥ | arvāca enānpatho bahujavāḥ kurudhvam | śṛṇuta dūtasya jagmuṣo no'syāgneḥ |", 'vājino vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 43 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 7.39.3: the bright Vasus played here on earth and in the wide mid-air; make your paths toward us. The Vājins.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.44 · The Vājins; the gods' wives"},
    {'padas': ['śaṃ no bhavantu vājino haveṣu devatātā mitadravaḥ svarkāḥ |', "jambhayanto'hiṃ vṛkaṃ rakṣāṃsi sanemyasmadyuyavannamīvāḥ ||", "sukhā no bhavantu vājino hvāneṣu devatātau yajñe | mitadravaḥ sumitadravaḥ | svarkāḥ svañcanā iti vā | svarcana iti vā | svarciṣa iti vā | jambhayanto'hiṃ ca vṛkaṃ ca rakṣāṃsi ca | kṣipramasmadyāvayantu | amīvā devāśvā iti vā |", 'devapatnyo devānāṃ patnyaḥ | tāsāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 44 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 7.38.7: may the swift Vājins be kind to us at our calls, crushing the serpent, wolf and demons. The wives of the gods.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "12.45 · The gods' wives"},
    {'padas': ['devānāṃ patnīruśatīravantu naḥ prāvantu nastujaye vājasātaye |', 'yāḥ pārthivāso yā apāmapi vrate tā no devīḥ suhavāḥ śarma yacchata ||', "devānāṃ patnya uśatyo'vantu naḥ | prāvantu naḥ | [ tujaye ] apatyajananāya cānnasaṃsananāya ca | yāḥ pārthivāso yā apāmapi vrate karmaṇi tā no devyaḥ suhavāḥ śarma yacchantu śaraṇam |", 'tāsāmeṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 45 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.46.7: may the eager wives of the gods help us, those of the earth and of the waters; give us shelter, goddesses.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '12.46 · Indrāṇī, Agnāyī, Aśvinī, Rāṭ, Rodasī, Varuṇānī'},
    {'padas': ['uta gnā vyantu devapatnīrindrāṇyagnāyyaśvinī rāṭ |', 'ā rodasī varuṇānī śṛṇotu vyantu devīrya ṛturjanīnām ||', 'api ca gnā vyantu devapatnyaḥ | indrāṇīndrasya patnī | agnāyyagneḥ patnī | aśvinyaśvinoḥ patnī | rāḍ rājate | rodasī rudrasya patnī | varuṇānī ca varuṇasya patnī | vyantu devyaḥ kāmayantāṃ ya ṛtukālo jāyānāṃ ya ṛtukālo jāyānām'], 'num': '|| 46 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.46.8: may the divine wives come, Indrāṇī, Agnāyī, Aśvinī, Rāṭ, Rodasī, Varuṇānī. The Daivata-kāṇḍa and the second half end.', 'prose': True},
    {'colophon': "|| iti dvādaśo'dhyāyaḥ ||", 'gloss': 'Thus the twelfth adhyāya.'},
    {'rubric': 'The khaṇḍānukramaṇī, the opening words of the forty-six khaṇḍas, which Sarup prints in brackets after the adhyāya.'},
    {'padas': ["[ athāto dyusthānā vasātiṣviheha jātā prātaryujā prātaryajadhvamuṣastaccitrametā utyāḥ sukiṃśukaṃ vṛṣākapāyyapāgūhaṃstvaṣṭā duhitre savitā viśvā rūpāṇi prātarjitamudu tyaṃ citraṃ śukraṃ te pathaspatha idaṃ viṣṇurviśvānaro vyākhyāto viśvānarasya yenā pāvaketi catuṣkaṃ keśyagniṃ trayaḥ keśinaḥ punarehi yasminvṛkṣe pāvīravī yadindrāgnī pavitravanta uta no'hiryāmatharvāthāto dyusthānā devagaṇā imā giraḥ sapta ṛṣayastiryagbilo devānāṃ bhadraumāso yajñena sugā vo devā jmayā atra śaṃ no bhavantu devānāṃ patnīruta gnā vyantviti ṣaṭcatvāriṃśat || ]"], 'num': '', 'gloss': '', 'prose': True},
